;; Groundwork's libraries, by side, and which others each may use.
;; test-code/groundwork/libraries_test.clj checks every namespace against it:
;; a library requires only the libraries it lists, and only their api;
;; nobody uses another around a circle. wire is a library of its own
;; (github.com/p4ulcristian/wire): any library may use it, through wire.api only.
;; So is cellar, Postgres (github.com/p4ulcristian/cellar): any server library
;; may use it, through cellar.api only. So is backroom, background jobs
;; (github.com/p4ulcristian/backroom): any server library may use it, through
;; backroom.api only. So is showroom, the browser build and the stylesheets it
;; bundles (github.com/p4ulcristian/showroom): only to build, never in
;; production, so no server namespace requires it (main loads it only when it
;; watches, by requiring-resolve); a browser namespace names its stylesheets
;; through showroom.api only. So is mailroom, how the browser and the server
;; talk, with a handler's steps and the routes (github.com/p4ulcristian/mailroom):
;; any library on either side may use it, through mailroom.api only.
{:server  {:sessions        #{}
           :access          #{}
           :sync            #{:access}
           :main            #{:sessions :access :sync}}
 :browser {:sync      #{}
           :main      #{:sync}}}
